From f204678b133688674cb853af088102ff387f1032 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: E-Vex <raiedaleve@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 08:29:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat(tools): the soak's crash telemetry is real -
 per-match panic isolation, seed attribution, and a report that survives the
 crash

The module docs promised A7 signals the code did not deliver: 'panics
surface as Err per match' was false (no catch_unwind anywhere - one
panic aborted the whole run, took the report and every later match's
telemetry with it, and the crashed counter was reachable only by
pre-simulation load errors). Every match now runs inside
catch_unwind (isolate_panic, with the written AssertUnwindSafe
soundness argument): a panic becomes one crashed count attributed to
its seed, the panic message lands in the report behind a 'panic:'
prefix, the sweep continues, the report prints, and main still exits
non-zero - isolation is observability, never recovery. SoakReport
gains the crashes field (seed + reason) and print_report lists them
(cap 10, a systematic storm cannot bury the summary). Seven new tests
(24 total, from 17): the sweep-seam regression injects a panicking
match and asserts it is counted, attributed, and survived - against
the pre-fix loop that test aborts (verified locally by temporarily
reverting the isolation); payload extraction, error-chain passthrough,
the cap, and an end-to-end real-content soak are pinned alongside.
